Dylan should be all over this momentarily. Yes,
IIUC, conflict _is_ line of sight, but it is not
"visible", only "potentially visible" that governs
(NetHack computes both mcansee and couldsee), which
is probably where the confusion arises. Conflict
works fine in pitch blackness, and on creatures with
no eyes, but doesn't work through walls.

I _think_ the appropriate code is that near line 609 of mon.c,

	if (Conflict && !mtmp->iswiz && mtmp->mcansee) {
/*...*/
